Algorithm 2: Estimating the average scale of target color blobs

Input : K-level image I (width W, height H), each level painted with a different (dominant) color, target color (level) C

Output: Estimate of average scale of C-colored blobs

1. Extract all blobs of color (level) C from image I and generate a binary image $I_{wat}$

2. Apply marker-controlled watershed segmentation to $I_{bw}$ to separate touching blobs;

3. Scan the segmented image $I_{wat}$ from top to bottom, and from left to right, separately;

4. In each scan line, collect all valid segmented lines belonging to the blobs;

5. Calculate the average $L_{h}$ and $L_{v}$ of all the horizontal and vertical blob lengths, respectively;

6. Linear scale of target color blobs $S_{C}=\sqrt{L_{h}\cdot L_{v}};$
